      "message": "**Location:** `util/focaltech/cli.cc` \\-\\\u003e `ParseCommand` and `ParseArguments`\n\n**The Issue:** The logic to detect if an argument is a firmware `.bin` file is duplicated across two functions. `ParseArguments` intercepts it, meaning the identical logic inside `ParseCommand` is dead code.\n\n**Remediation:** Remove the duplicated check from `ParseArguments` and trust `ParseCommand` to do its job.\n\n```c\n  // Delete this entire block from ParseArguments:\n  /*\n  if (first_arg.ends_with(\".bin\")) {\n    config.cmd \u003d Command::kUpdate;\n    config.ec_bin \u003d first_arg;\n    return config;\n  }\n  */\n\n  // Replace with this streamlined flow:\n  config.cmd \u003d ParseCommand(first_arg);\n  \n  if (config.cmd \u003d\u003d Command::kUnknown) {\n    FT_LOGE(\"Unknown subcommand: {}\", first_arg);\n    return std::unexpected(Error::kParameterError);\n  }\n\n  if (config.cmd \u003d\u003d Command::kUpdate) {\n    config.ec_bin \u003d first_arg;\n  }\n\n```",
