      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini identified these locations:\n\n----\n\nApplying \"const-correctness\" to local variables is one of the most effective ways to improve C++ code readability. When a reviewer or maintainer sees `const auto` or `const type`, they immediately know they don\u0027t have to track the state of that variable for the rest of the scope.\n\nI\u0027ve gone through the entire codebase and identified every local variable that is initialized and **never mutated** afterward.\n\nHere is the exhaustive list of places to add `const`, organized by file:\n\n### **`util/focaltech/cli.cc`**\n\n* `auto lower \u003d ToLower(arg);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto lower \u003d ...`\n* `auto [ptr, ec] \u003d std::from_chars(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto [ptr, ec] \u003d ...` *(Yes, structured bindings can be const!)*\n* `std::string_view first_arg \u003d args[0];` $\\rightarrow$ `const std::string_view first_arg \u003d ...`\n* `auto wp_res \u003d ParseWpArea(args[1]);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto wp_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto wp_res \u003d GetFlashProtection(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto wp_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto fw_data_res \u003d ReadFileToVector(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto fw_data_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto res \u003d UpdateFw(...)` *(Inside the `for` loop init-statement)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto res \u003d ...`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/updater.cc`**\n\n* `uint32_t pages \u003d ...` $\\rightarrow$ `const uint32_t pages \u003d ...`\n* `size_t file_len \u003d buffer.size();` $\\rightarrow$ `const size_t file_len \u003d ...`\n* `auto erase_res \u003d ErasePage(...)` *(Both instances in `DownloadBin` and `ReturnToRomBoot`)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto erase_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto page_res \u003d DownloadPage(...)` *(All three instances in `DownloadBin`)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto page_res \u003d ...`\n* `uint8_t hash_mode \u003d ...` $\\rightarrow$ `const uint8_t hash_mode \u003d ...`\n* `auto io_res \u003d ReceiveBulkDataIn(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto io_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto local_hash \u003d CalculateSha256(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto local_hash \u003d ...`\n* `auto config_res \u003d HasValidConfigPage(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto config_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto res \u003d ResetMcu(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto res \u003d ...`\n* `auto res \u003d ReceiveBulkDataIn(...)` *(In `GetFlashProtection` and `SetFlashProtection`)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto res \u003d ...`\n* `auto wp_area \u003d static_cast\u003cFlashWpArea\u003e(data[0]);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto wp_area \u003d ...`\n* `auto get_res \u003d GetFlashProtection(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto get_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto reset_res \u003d ResetMcu(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto reset_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto cmd \u003d BuildFtCmd(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto cmd \u003d ...`\n* `auto null_pos \u003d std::ranges::find(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto null_pos \u003d ...`\n* `std::string version(data.begin(), null_pos);` $\\rightarrow$ `const std::string version(...)`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/ft_scsi.cc`**\n\n* `BulkCbWrap cbw{...};` $\\rightarrow$ `const BulkCbWrap cbw{...};`\n* `auto cbw_span \u003d AsUint8Span(cbw);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto cbw_span \u003d ...`\n* `auto send_res \u003d device.Send(...)` *(Both instances)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto send_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto csw_span \u003d AsWritableUint8Span(csw);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto csw_span \u003d ...` *(The span itself is const, even though the underlying data it points to is mutable).*\n* `auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(...)` *(Both instances)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto recv_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto cbw_res \u003d SendCbw(...)` *(Both instances)* $\\rightarrow$ `const auto cbw_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto res \u003d device.WaitForReset(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto res \u003d ...`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/libusb_transport.cc`**\n\n* `ssize_t count \u003d libusb_get_device_list(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const ssize_t count \u003d ...`\n* `auto devices \u003d std::span(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto devices \u003d ...`\n* `auto found \u003d FindFocalDevice(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto found \u003d ...`\n* `auto open_res \u003d transport.Open();` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto open_res \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_open(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `auto ep_info \u003d FindBulkEndpoints(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto ep_info \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_set_auto_detach_kernel_driver(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_bulk_transfer(...)` *(In both `Send` and `Recv`)* $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_get_configuration(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_reset_device(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `int r \u003d libusb_release_interface(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const int r \u003d ...`\n* `UsbDeviceId current_id{...}` $\\rightarrow$ `const UsbDeviceId current_id{...}`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/ft_util.cc`**\n\n* `auto size \u003d file.tellg();` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto size \u003d ...`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/main.cc`**\n\n* `std::vector\u003cstd::string_view\u003e args(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const std::vector\u003cstd::string_view\u003e args(...)`\n* `auto config \u003d focaltech::ParseArguments(args);` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto config \u003d ...`\n* `auto mode_res \u003d focaltech::GetDeviceMode(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto mode_res \u003d ...`\n* `auto exec_res \u003d focaltech::ExecuteCommand(...)` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto exec_res \u003d ...`\n\n### **`util/focaltech/ft_log.h`**\n\n* `auto now \u003d std::chrono::system_clock::now();` $\\rightarrow$ `const auto now \u003d ...`",
