      "message": "Now that we changed to strings `ParseInt` is never used and can be removed:\n\n----\n\n\n\n### **Dead Code Elimination: `ParseInt`**\n\n**Location:** `util/focaltech/cli.h`, `cli.cc`, and `cli_test.cc`\n\n**The Issue:** The `ParseInt` function is fully implemented using `\u003ccharconv\u003e` and has its own dedicated unit tests (`ParseInt_Valid`, `ParseInt_Negative`, `ParseInt_Invalid`). However, it is **never actually called** anywhere in the application. The current command set only parses file paths and the string enums (`none`, `boot`, `ro`, `all`).\n\n**Remediation:** Code that isn\u0027t executed is a maintenance burden. Delete the `ParseInt` declaration, definition, and unit tests entirely. If a future command requires integer parsing, it can be added back via version control.",
