      "message": "### **DRY Up the Logging Macro Branching**\n\n**Location:** `util/focaltech/ft_log.h` -\u003e `FtLog`\n\n**The Issue:** The `FtLog` function has redundant branching to handle terminal coloring. It explicitly checks if `color` is empty to decide which format string to use:\n\n```cpp\n  if (!color.empty()) {\n    std::print(\"{}[{:%m-%d %H:%M:%S}] {} [{}][{}:{}] \", color, now, level_str, log::kLogTag, file, loc.line());\n  } else {\n    std::print(\"[{:%m-%d %H:%M:%S}] {} [{}][{}:{}] \", now, level_str, log::kLogTag, file, loc.line());\n  }\n\n```\n\n**Remediation:** Since `color` defaults to an empty `std::string_view` when disabled, `std::print` will safely and cleanly substitute nothing for the first argument. You can delete the `else` branch completely:\n\n```cpp\n  std::print(\"{}[{:%m-%d %H:%M:%S}] {} [{}][{}:{}] \", color, now, level_str, log::kLogTag, file, loc.line());\n  \n  std::println(fmt, std::forward\u003cArgs\u003e(args)...);\n  \n  // Only the reset sequence needs an explicit check\n  if (!color.empty()) {\n    std::print(\"{}\", kColorReset);\n  }\n\n```",
