      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini instructions:\n\n----\n\nBy defining a custom GoogleMock action, we can condense six lines of repetitive lambda boilerplate into a single, highly readable `.WillOnce(ReturnValidCsw(1))` statement.\n\n*(Note: We will specifically skip refactoring the tests `SendBulkDataOut_CswSignatureMismatch` and `ReceiveBulkDataIn_FailsOnNonZeroCswStatus`. Since those tests are explicitly designed to test **invalid** CSW responses, they should keep their custom lambdas!)*\n\nHere are the exact changes needed across the three files:\n\n### **1. Define the GMock Action in `test_utils.h**`\n\n**File:** `util/focaltech/test_utils.h`\nFirst, ensure you include the GMock header, and then define the action using the `ACTION_P` macro (which stands for \"Action with 1 Parameter\").\n\nAdd this near the bottom of `focaltech::testing` namespace:\n\n```cpp\n#include \u003cgmock/gmock.h\u003e\n\n// ... existing BuildValidCsw function ...\n\n// Custom GMock action to populate the buffer with a valid CSW and return the size.\nACTION_P(ReturnValidCsw, tag) {\n  // \u0027arg0\u0027 magically represents the first argument passed to Recv() (the std::span)\n  focaltech::testing::BuildValidCsw(arg0, tag);\n  return std::expected\u003csize_t, focaltech::Error\u003e(focaltech::testing::kUsbCswSize);\n}\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Clean up `ft_scsi_test.cc**`\n\n**File:** `util/focaltech/ft_scsi_test.cc`\nYou need to add `using focaltech::testing::ReturnValidCsw;` at the top of your test file or just reference it directly. Replace the verbose `Invoke` blocks in these three tests:\n\n**In `SendBulkDataOut_DataOutSuccess`:**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Recv(_, _))\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Recv(_, _)).WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1));\n\n```\n\n**In `ReceiveBulkDataIn_Success`:**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n      .WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1));\n\n```\n\n**In `ReceiveBulkDataIn_EmptyBuffer`:**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Recv(_, _))\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Recv(_, _)).WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1));\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Clean up `updater_test.cc**`\n\n**File:** `util/focaltech/updater_test.cc`\nSimilarly, replace the blocks in the following three tests.\n\n**In `GetFlashProtection_Success`:**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n      .WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1));\n\n```\n\n**In `SetFlashProtection_Success` (Two Replacements):**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }))\n  // ...\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 2);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n      .WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1))\n  // ...\n      .WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(2));\n\n```\n\n**In `ReturnToRomBoot_Success`:**\n\n```cpp\n  // Old:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_ptr, Recv(_, _))\n      .WillOnce(Invoke(\n          [](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n            testing::BuildValidCsw(data, 1);\n            return testing::kUsbCswSize;\n          }));\n\n  // New:\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_ptr, Recv(_, _)).WillOnce(testing::ReturnValidCsw(1));\n\n```",
