      "message": "**Location:** `util/focaltech/main.cc`\n\n**The Issue:** When you check if a `std::expected` contains a value, using `.value()` to extract it is technically correct, but it is considered overly verbose and visually noisy in modern C++.\n\n**Remediation:** Since the preceding `if (!transport)` check proves the value exists, you can safely and idiomatically use the dereference operator (`*`) just like you would with an `std::optional` or a smart pointer.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n```c\n  // Old:\n  focaltech::UsbDevice usb_device(std::make_unique\u003cfocaltech::LibusbTransport\u003e(\n      std::move(transport.value())));\n      \n  if (auto exec_res \u003d\n          focaltech::ExecuteCommand(config.value(), usb_device, *mode_res);\n\n  // New:\n  focaltech::UsbDevice usb_device(std::make_unique\u003cfocaltech::LibusbTransport\u003e(\n      std::move(*transport)));\n      \n  if (auto exec_res \u003d focaltech::ExecuteCommand(*config, usb_device, *mode_res);\n\n```",
