      "message": "**Location:** `util/focaltech/updater.cc` \\-\\\u003e `SetFlashProtection`\n\n**The Issue:** `FlashWpArea` is strictly defined as an `enum class FlashWpArea : uint32_t`. Calling `std::to_underlying` on it already yields a `uint32_t`. Wrapping that in `static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(...)` adds visual noise with no functional benefit. Furthermore, applying the bitwise NOT operator (`~`) to a `uint32_t` results in an `unsigned int` (which is standardly a `uint32_t`), making the second cast redundant as well.\n\n**Remediation:** Remove the `static_cast` wrappers.\n\n```c\n  // Old:\n  .address \u003d static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(std::to_underlying(wp_area)),\n  .length \u003d static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(~std::to_underlying(wp_area)),\n\n  // New:\n  .address \u003d std::to_underlying(wp_area),\n  .length \u003d ~std::to_underlying(wp_area),\n\n```",
