      "message": "Gemini instructions:\n\n----\n\nThe trailing return types on lambdas (`-\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e`) are exclusively found inside the `Invoke` blocks for `MockUsbTransport` calls.\n\nThey appear in exactly two files: **`ft_scsi_test.cc`** and **`updater_test.cc`**.\n\nHere is the exact list of the 12 instances you will need to update across those two files:\n\n### **In `util/focaltech/ft_scsi_test.cc` (6 instances):**\n\n1. `SendBulkDataOut_DataOutSuccess` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n2. `SendBulkDataOut_CswSignatureMismatch` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n3. `ReceiveBulkDataIn_Success` (mocking `Recv` for data)\n4. `ReceiveBulkDataIn_Success` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n5. `ReceiveBulkDataIn_EmptyBuffer` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n6. `ReceiveBulkDataIn_FailsOnNonZeroCswStatus` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n\n### **In `util/focaltech/updater_test.cc` (6 instances):**\n\n7. `GetFlashProtection_Success` (mocking `Recv` for data)\n8. `GetFlashProtection_Success` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n9. `SetFlashProtection_Success` (mocking `Recv` for first CSW)\n10. `SetFlashProtection_Success` (mocking `Recv` for data)\n11. `SetFlashProtection_Success` (mocking `Recv` for second CSW)\n12. `ReturnToRomBoot_Success` (mocking `Recv` for CSW)\n\nFor all of these, you can simply delete the `-\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e` and let C++14/C++23 do the type deduction for you!",
