      "message": "### **Modernize Sub-Range Manipulations in Tests**\n\n**Location:** `util/focaltech/usb_device_test.cc` and `updater_test.cc`\n\n**The Issue:** There are a few places in the tests where memory buffers are filled using raw iterator arithmetic (e.g., `buffer.begin() + offset`). This is a C++98 pattern that is prone to off-by-one errors and out-of-bounds access if the math is wrong.\n\n**Remediation:** Use C++20 `std::ranges` along with span slicing methods to modify subsets of the data declaratively and safely.\n\n**Changes in `usb_device_test.cc`:**\n\n```c\n  // Old:\n  std::fill(data.begin(), data.begin() + 5, 0xAB);\n  \n  // New:\n  std::ranges::fill(data.first(5), 0xAB);\n\n```",
